The '''Torre CIEA''' is a 75-storey office tower under construction at 400 [[Avinguda Embarcadero]] in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. The tower is being developed by [[CIEA]], the largest energy company in Balboa, as its new corporate headquarters. Construction began in 2023, with completion estimated for 2028. At a planned height of 350 metres (1,148 ft), the Torre CIEA will become the tallest building in Balboa upon completion, surpassing the [[Torre CBNM]] (270 metres).

The tower replaces the company's former headquarters, the old Torre CIEA at 20 Carrer Verd, which has been renamed and now operates as a multi-tenant office building.

== History ==

CIEA had been headquartered at the original Torre CIEA (now [[20 Carrer Verd]]) since the 1980s. By the 2020s, the company had outgrown the 40-storey tower and announced plans for a new headquarters building on the Avinguda Embarcadero waterfront. The site at 400 Avinguda Embarcadero was assembled from parcels acquired between 2019 and 2022.

Construction began in 2023. The project is one of the largest commercial developments undertaken in Sant Cristòfor since the [[Balboa real-estate bubble|real-estate bubble]] era, and the first building in the city to target a height of 350 metres.

Upon completion, the Torre CIEA will be the tallest building in Balboa, the tallest building in Sant Cristòfor, and the tallest building in Original, surpassing the [[Torre CBNM]] by approximately 80 metres.

